                <pb facs="0743" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.3911/2a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-04T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4,
                                1924—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Please transmit the following confidential message to General Vasquez from
                    Mr. Welles: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In accordance with our conversation the night prior to my departure from
                            Santo Domingo, I trust that it will be possible for you and the members
                            of the party which you have selected to visit Washington during the
                            present month. I have ascertained that the most desirable time for your
                            visit would be during the week commencing <pb facs="0744" n="630"
                                xml:id="pg630"/> June 23rd. As you know, I attribute the greatest
                            importance to the opportunity which your visit here will afford for the
                            reaching of an agreement in principle regarding the various matters
                            which we have discussed. I shall be grateful if you will advise me, by
                            cable through the American Legation, as soon as you have determined the
                            date of your departure and the steamer upon which you are sailing in
                            order that I may make appropriate arrangements. Please accept my most
                            cordial greetings.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
